  "generated_note": "Automated Friday run (2026-11-06) pulled live from Metricool per AUTOMATION.md, window Oct 30 - Nov 5, 2026 (this run's own Step 1 window, 14 properties post-merge).\n\nDATA QUALITY (posts_channels): used getScheduledPosts (PUBLISHED, in-window, per-property local timezone, extendedRange) as ground truth for every property's Facebook/Instagram/TikTok/Google Business posts_channels count, not the evolution SUM fields -- consistent with the documented day-mislabeling issues in those fields. Capri Palms' getScheduledPosts came back empty despite real TikTok activity in the evolution connector (1 video, 66 interactions, 915 views) -- per the explicit fallback rule, used the evolution SUM count for this one property: Capri Palms posts_channels={TikTok:1}.\n\nTIKTOK AUTO-PUBLISH FAILURES (flag for Val): Residences at the Overlook had one TikTok post error on first attempt (Nov 3, \"incorrect content format\") but succeeded on a manual retry the next day (Nov 4) -- counted the successful retry, not the failed attempt. Santa Fe had a TikTok post fail outright on Nov 5 with \"Could not refresh TikTok Business accessToken\" -- this looks like an expired/revoked TikTok connection for Santa Fe specifically, not a one-off content issue, and has no successful retry on record. Worth checking Santa Fe's TikTok connection in Metricool directly.\n\nDATA ANOMALY UPDATE (Villa Siena, improving): Facebook followers continued a modest climb this week (271 -> 274, +3) but did NOT repeat the previous two weeks' sharp jumps (80->231, 231->271) -- growth this week is in a normal/plausible range. Still worth a manual check against Villa Siena's real Facebook page follower count at some point, but no longer flagging this as urgent.\n\nGBP WINDOW: ran the full walk-back/completeness check. This run's own window (Oct 30-Nov 5) returned essentially no data (1/7 days, all zero) -- expected, normal pre-sync state. Walked back to Oct 23-29 (last run's own window): still genuinely incomplete (2-5 of 7 days per property, confirmed via identical retry on two properties -- not the query-merge bug). Walked back one more week to Oct 16-22: reconfirmed fully complete (7/7 days, all 13 GBP-connected properties) and verified identical to the already-published figures (spot-checked Lakeside/Lakeview exactly). GBP_CURRENT stays at Oct 16-22, 2026 for a 3rd consecutive run -- not a stall, this window is simply stable and mature now. GBP_PRIOR re-pulled fresh for Oct 9-15, 2026 (confirmed complete, 7/7 days): reach_search/reach_maps/website_clicks/directions_clicks all matched the previously-derived baseline exactly (5314/1378/577/626), but phone_clicks came back 280 this run -- reverting from last run's 277 back to the original 280. This specific field continues to show small +/-3 unit intraday/multi-day volatility on this now-3-week-old window even though every other field has fully stabilized; not treating it as an error, just re-using whatever the live pull shows each time. Because GBP_CURRENT itself is unchanged (still Oct 16-22 vs Oct 9-15), every GMB tile's current value is identical to last week; only phone_clicks' delta shifts from -37 back to -40 to reflect the revised prior-week baseline. posts_published unchanged (GBP_CURRENT=8, GBP_PRIOR=6) -- not re-verified via getScheduledPosts a third time since the window itself didn't change and this field isn't subject to backfill lag. Views KPI, views_by_channel, and every property's views_channels/top_channel recomputed this run using the unchanged GBP Reach proxy; engagement KPI and the Google Business engagement_by_channel entry use the unchanged GBP clicks total (1,502).\n\nURL Tracking: no new GA4 export this week -- carried forward unchanged from last week's real Oct 22-29 reading (applied 2026-10-30), delta zeroed. GMB URL Tracking is still held pending a window match: gbp_window_label is still \"Oct 16 - 22, 2026\", so the real Oct 22-29 GMB numbers documented in last week's generated_note (portfolio: views 3192, sessions 437, engaged_sessions 353, key_events 16; full by-property breakdown there, including the Claxton Pointe & Pecan Ridge / Lamar Lofts \"1-2/2\" pagination caveat) remain unapplied and should be used once gbp_window_label finally advances to \"Oct 22 - 29, 2026\" in a future run. Facebook Groups stays at 0/0 (unchanged, still manual-only).\n\nGBP WINDOW ADVANCED 2026-11-06 (after Val manually triggered a GMB resync 2026-10-30): Oct 23-29, 2026 (this run's own window) now passes the completeness test -- 7/7 days, all 13 GBP-connected properties, confirmed live. GBP_CURRENT advances from Oct 16-22 to Oct 22-29 (no longer lagging); GBP_PRIOR advances to Oct 16-22 (re-pulled fresh, not reused -- all 5 fields matched the already-published Oct 16-22 figures exactly, confirming stability). New posts_published 5 (verified via getScheduledPosts; was 8), reach_search 5,165 (-135), reach_maps 1,360 (+16), website_clicks 517 (-73), phone_clicks 218 (-22), directions_clicks 716 (+44). Views KPI, views_by_channel, and every property's views_channels/top_channel recomputed with the new GBP Reach proxy; engagement KPI and the Google Business engagement_by_channel entry recomputed with the new GBP clicks total. Google Business URL Tracking (gmb_url_tracking) applied for the first time with a real export now that its window matches gbp_window_label exactly -- see that section's own note for detail. Facebook Groups URL Tracking (url_tracking) carries forward last week's now-corrected Oct 22-29 reading (Landings and Hills at Hoover were revised slightly after a second, more complete GA4 export; see data/week-2026-10-29.json's url_tracking note).",
